            <title>[IGNITE-6002] Make log message more pretty when instance name is null</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-6002</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When instance name is null, log message containing &quot;null&quot; is shown like as follows.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;[09-08-2017 14:49:38][INFO ][grid-timeout-worker-#15%&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;%][IgniteKernal]
Metrics &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; local node (to disable set &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&apos;metricsLogFrequency&apos;&lt;/span&gt; to 0)
    ^-- Node [id=de0743ec, name=&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;, uptime=00:01:00:007]
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
